{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat ../research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_19-27-07-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/audit-spec/v1.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A client proposal allocates its origin row slot and establishes command/Seq/Deps at its owner. PreAccept receivers qualify ballot and merge local conflicts, reporting current value ballot and status. Matching replies supply the fast threshold; initial ballot plus equality and large-N committed-dependency conditions permit direct commit, otherwise Accept is broadcast and matching majority replies commit. Commit propagates the full tuple. Execution waits for committed dependency graph and orders SCCs before application and default client response.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-client\",\n        \"B-phase1\",\n        \"B-accept\",\n        \"B-commit\",\n        \"B-execute\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-record\",\n        \"F-decision\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-accept\",\n        \"S-attrs\",\n        \"S-base\",\n        \"S-client\",\n        \"S-commit\",\n        \"S-exec\",\n        \"S-loop\",\n        \"S-preaccept\",\n        \"S-recovery\",\n        \"S-send\",\n        \"S-state\",\n        \"S-types\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Authority is per instance, not solely the master-selected leader. Initial ballot equals origin replica; recovery replaces leader bookkeeping and chooses a ballot based on proposer id and, when IsLeader, maxRecvBallot. Prepare raises the local promise and returns prior value ballot/status; formation rejects older requests and reply handlers qualify lastTriedBallot/phase. Execution detects incomplete work and queues recovery. Prepare quorum selection adopts highest value-ballot record and chooses committed installation, Accept, or restarted phase1; old client proposals are retained. Already committed records resist subsequent Accept and Commit replacement.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-authority\",\n        \"B-recover-select\",\n        \"B-membership\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-record\",\n        \"F-decision\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-accept\",\n        \"S-ballot\",\n        \"S-base\",\n        \"S-commit\",\n        \"S-config\",\n        \"S-exec\",\n        \"S-loop\",\n        \"S-master\",\n        \"S-preaccept\",\n        \"S-recovery\",\n        \"S-send\",\n        \"S-transport\",\n        \"S-try\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Formation writes the same tuple and status that Prepare exposes to new owners. bal qualifies old requests while vbal and Status determine how old support is interpreted during recovery. Acks can contribute to local commit even though the receiver Accept path does not change Status; this discrepancy is retained rather than assuming an acceptance guarantee. Commit and execution establish prior decisions that restrict later handlers. Per-message delay goroutines mean pending messages can overlap authority changes; no FIFO handler-delivery assumption is used.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-phase1\",\n        \"B-accept\",\n        \"B-authority\",\n        \"B-recover-select\",\n        \"B-commit\",\n        \"B-execute\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-record\",\n        \"F-decision\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-accept\",\n        \"S-attrs\",\n        \"S-ballot\",\n        \"S-base\",\n        \"S-commit\",\n        \"S-exec\",\n        \"S-loop\",\n        \"S-preaccept\",\n        \"S-recovery\",\n        \"S-send\",\n        \"S-state\",\n        \"S-transport\",\n        \"S-try\",\n        \"S-types\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Legal recovery histories for missing ACCEPTED status and changed local value ballot.\",\n      \"Quorum-size applicability across N; duplicate reply support assumptions.\",\n      \"SCAN conflict coverage, SCC tie-break reachability and optional persistence obligations.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Both core relationships and their connection have been traced through source, including fixed membership, network dispatch, recovery and consumption. Local discrepancies remain questions, not asserted defects.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"1f9ed13fa4254b83b4e7346a0d9aa103\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"1f9ed13fa4254b83b4e7346a0d9aa103\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"next_objective\": {\n    \"action\": \"investigate_and_refocus\",\n    \"boundary\": \"both_core_paths\",\n    \"reason\": \"Use results to update understanding and compare the remaining frontier\",\n    \"core_gaps\": []\n  },\n  \"drafts\": [],\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"eee4de64737240419ebf2cd5af7bae73\",\n      \"question\": {\n        \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n        \"disposition\": \"concrete_suspicion\",\n        \"preferred_check\": \"controlled_schedule\",\n        \"question\": \"After a nonstale Accept is acknowledged, can recovery reliably distinguish and preserve its accepted tuple when handleAccept leaves Status unchanged?\",\n        \"importance\": \"If acknowledged accepted support is reinterpreted as preaccepted or absent, a later owner may select inconsistent ordering attributes or commands, threatening per-instance agreement. This is a potential consequence, not an observed violation.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"S-accept\",\n          \"S-attrs\",\n          \"S-ballot\",\n          \"S-base\",\n          \"S-commit\",\n          \"S-config\",\n          \"S-exec\",\n          \"S-loop\",\n          \"S-master\",\n          \"S-preaccept\",\n          \"S-recovery\",\n          \"S-send\",\n          \"S-state\",\n          \"S-transport\",\n          \"S-try\",\n          \"S-types\"\n        ],\n        \"participants\": [\n          \"Initial instance owner\",\n          \"Accept receiver\",\n          \"Recovery owner and Prepare quorum\"\n        ],\n        \"objects\": [\n          \"Instance record and PrepareReply\"\n        ],\n        \"contexts\": [\n          \"Fixed membership and constructor-enforced thriftiness\",\n          \"Crash-stop and delayed messages; no arbitrary duplicate RPC injection\"\n        ],\n        \"event_paths\": [\n          \"startPhase1 -> PreAcceptReply -> bcastAccept -> handleAccept -> handlePrepare -> handlePrepareReply\"\n        ],\n        \"activity_classes\": [\n          \"A1\",\n          \"A2\",\n          \"A3\"\n        ],\n        \"behavior_ids\": [\n          \"B-accept\",\n          \"B-authority\",\n          \"B-recover-select\"\n        ],\n        \"fact_ids\": [\n          \"F-record\"\n        ],\n        \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n          \"B-phase1\": \"Produces the proposal and slow-path Accept preceding the investigated acknowledgement.\",\n          \"B-membership\": \"Defines quorum sizes and transport delivery constraints.\",\n          \"B-execute\": \"Queues recovery for incomplete instances.\"\n        },\n        \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"recovery\",\n        \"counterevidence\": [\n          \"Accept updates both ballot fields and ordering attributes; absence of a status update alone does not prove information loss.\",\n          \"Prepare returns commands and attributes in addition to Status; highest-value-ballot selection may preserve the same tuple.\",\n          \"Commit delivery and already-committed guards may prevent divergence in histories where a decision was propagated.\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Which legal crash/delay history exposes the status distinction after a completed slow-path acknowledgement?\",\n          \"Does a sourced local acceptance/recovery responsibility suffice, or is a same-history divergence needed to establish the intended guarantee?\"\n        ],\n        \"priority\": 3,\n        \"trigger_rationale\": \"The receiver records Accept attributes without recording ACCEPTED, while the directly downstream recovery switch explicitly assigns accepted and preaccepted records different continuation paths. Source and a small controlled history can discriminate this; a costly cluster-wide test is premature. Persistence is lower priority because default durability is disabled; quorum sizing is retained as another relationship.\"\n      },\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n      \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n      \"stop_reason\": \"Record the two core relationship